      "name": null,
      "problem": "Factor the polynomial expression $x(w-6)-10(w-6).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(x(w-6),10(w-6))=w-6\n$$\n\nEach term is already written as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (w-6)-10\\cdot (w-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (w-6)-10\\cdot (w-6) & = \\\\ (x-10)(w-6) & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
